  "label": "Computational Biomolecular Prediction Validation",
  "related": [
    "models-ai-protein-6464",
    "infection-host-a1f2",
    "rna-binding-139a"
  ],
  "secondary_categories": [
    "genomics"
  ],
  "slug": "confidence-ordering-contextual-68b5",
  "summary": "Side-chain optimization, metadynamics, and protonation-state analyses now test predictions against structures, benchmarks, and energetics.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is computational modeling of biomolecular structure and energetics, with explicit benchmarking in only some items. The kinase study applies MCCE analysis to 37 cocrystal structures and finds that inhibitor binding shifts protonation and tautomeric states, altering bound-state energetics. The c-MYC study combines well-tempered metadynamics and all-atom MD to map a conformational landscape and identify drugging pockets, then docks inhibitor 10074-G5 over 1 μs. The quantum annealing study benchmarks a D-Wave hybrid solver against Gurobi on 40 protein side-chain optimization instances. The TP53 preprint is exploratory, relating von Neumann entropy from a quantum harmonic oscillator model to hot spots with n=6. What is new is treating bound-state chemical states as energetic variables and casting side-chain placement as a combinatorial optimization benchmarked against a classical solver.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-10"
}
